  <h2>Global synthesis</h2>
  <p>Each edition delivers one deep analysis and two concise signals drawn from a global ring of 32 primary research feeds. We focus on research at the edge of human vitality: quantum biology, cellular senolytics, NRF-2 activation, brain connectomics, and daily functional health.</p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>Our intelligence pipeline monitors global preprints (arXiv, bioRxiv, medRxiv), clinical trial databases, and leading peer-reviewed journals. We screen candidates through a high-signal novelty filter to eliminate press release noise and isolate break-through findings.</p>

  <p>Every brief explicitly cites and links its original sources. Agewell Brief adds historical biophysical lineage, multi-layer context, and practical takeaways—never aggregated clickbait.</p>

  <h2 id="editorial-desk">The editorial desk</h2>
  <p><strong>Agewell Brief Editorial Desk</strong> combines systematic source monitoring with layered human review before anything publishes, under unified global editorial accountability.</p>

  <h2>What we believe</h2>
  <p>Aging is not an inevitable decline into medical dependency. Our readers across the world are capable adults with sharp judgment and vast potential ahead. We write accordingly: direct science, original sources, and empowering global clarity.</p>
